{"candidates":[{"file":"src/mail/mail.service.ts","symbol":"MailService.confirmNewEmail","start_line":136,"end_line":141,"explanation":"The verification link for a changed email is built with the path '/confirm-email'. That is the same frontend page the sign-up activation mail (userSignUp) uses. It should point to a dedicated '/confirm-new-email' page. The page the link opens is the sign-up confirmation page, which presumably calls POST /auth/email/confirm (AuthService.confirmEmail). That endpoint only accepts users whose status is inactive and ignores the newEmail claim in the token. An active user changing their email therefore gets a 404 or an error, and the email is never changed. The correct page would call /auth/email/confirm/new, which is handled by AuthService.confirmNewEmail."}],"fix":{"file":"src/mail/mail.service.ts","description":"In MailService.confirmNewEmail, change the URL path from '/confirm-email' to '/confirm-new-email'. The frontend page at that path can then call the confirm-new-email endpoint.","replacement_code":"    const url = new URL(
      this.configService.getOrThrow('app.frontendDomain', {
        infer: true,
      }) + '/confirm-new-email',
    );"}}

fix.replacement_code:
const url = new URL(
  this.configService.getOrThrow('app.frontendDomain', {
    infer: true,
  }) + '/confirm-new-email',
);

